%% element $g\in G$ verifies $\LM(g)=X^{i_3}$,
%% and therefore $\min(\l G\r) = \{ X_3^{i_3}\}$.
%% 
%% Because the ideal $I$ of vanishing polynomials on $V$ is of dimension zero,
%% there is a polynomial $f$ in any minimal Gr\"obner basis $\G_3$
%% of $I$ such that $\LM(f)=X_3^\ell$ for some
%% $\ell>0$. Given $\beta=(\beta_1,\beta_2)\in \pi_2(V)$, the fiber $V[\beta]$
%% has cardinal $i_3$, and because $f(\beta,X_3)=X_3^\ell +\cdots$ must vanish
%% on $V[\beta]$, one sees that necessarily $\ell \ge i_3$. But since
%% $g\in I$, there exists a polynomial $h$ in $\G_3$ such that $\LM(h)|\LM(g)$,
