codex
The substantive v2 confirms the family is natively “finite point set → lexicographic Gröbner basis,” and it explicitly names efficient reconstruction methods (Buchberger–Möller, Lederer, and the lex game); the paper itself leaves its complexity section unfinished. So Track A is untenable. I’m now testing the only viable alternative: whether a Track B construction can create a large measured gap between exact reconstruction and a short structural route without relying on the withdrawn decomposition. If that gap cannot be demonstrated, the correct deliverable is a reviewable rejection with both costs.
