The bare loop hardened only at order 10: all three oracles failed on 10,000 points, while every lower rung had at least one verified solution. I’m now sliding the named ladder to orders 6/8/10 as the harness requires. At this shipping size, cubic Buchberger–Möller is no longer executable in a local gate, so I’m adding the paper-native mechanical reference that exhaustively builds every projection-fiber table and verifies the resulting circuits. It still solves every instance, has a measured linear-in-input cost at shipping, and is distinct from the compact route, which inspects only one informative fiber per coordinate. The smaller 256-point Buchberger–Möller measurement will remain as a calibration, not be misreported as shipping cost.
