codex
Implemented and verified a native Track B generator.

Key results:

- Shipping preset: 10,000 points over `GF(2013265921)`
- All G1–G9 gates pass
- Structured guesses: 0/200,000
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 each
- Reference algorithm: 541,029 operations median
- Compact fiber route: ≤235 operations
- Bare oracle: 0/3 solved
- Structural/placebo arms: both 1/3 solved
- Answer bound: 317 characters, 24 atoms

The [paper is withdrawn](https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.3887) because its central decomposition is flawed. The generator explicitly avoids that theorem and uses an independently verified inverse construction.

Deliverables:

- [gen_1207_3887.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.3887/gen_1207_3887.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.3887/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.3887/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.3887/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.3887/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1207.3887/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The README documents the withdrawal, exact construction proof, full oracle ladder, and the caveat that one shipping failure was an empty provider response rather than an explicit wrong witness.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
